From a33755953d562804c0b79eb0eb6d336f5bc1ee97 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 22:54:36 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 10210/11362] Correct seven artifacts: finished runs
 reclassified partial -> null

Companion to f5f4364cc6 (the writer fixes). Each artifact declared
verdict_class partial while its own gate evidence shows the run
finished (ready scores 1.0, all-gates-passed, full task/branch
matrices). REQ-CONDUCTOR-VERDICT-3: partial means may-retry; a
finished run with a mixed or absent effect is null.

Append-only per the corrigendum pattern: every artifact gains a dated
verdict_class_correction_note_2026_08_28 preserving the original
status, honest_verdict, and class verbatim; checksums recomputed with
each module's own function; module validators re-run clean. Mirror
rows for exp6506/exp6510 inside exp6510/exp6513/exp6526 follow the
same-day upstream corrections and are itemized in each note. exp6687's
flagged_adversarial stamp (cause: NONTERMINAL_DECLARED_ARTIFACT from
the corrected partial declaration) is preserved untouched; clearing it
is the gate owner's call and the note says so.

adversarial_verify after correction: 0 flags on five artifacts; the
pre-existing SUBSTRATE_NO_LLM_BY_NAME warn on exp6659/exp6687 is
unrelated to this change. VERDICT_PREFIX_CLASS_CONTRADICTION no longer
fires on any of the seven.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JntPrUGLNesPcJH1pyfFYw
